[[:db/retract 17592186096937 :question/answer-fields 17592186093596] {:db/id 17592186096459 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n![](images/b3/b3512e604d6c4246c5582a75360076115c4bd9b6701c42587f318254b1c026a3.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/76/765eafb8a8b60aec9af512eeb666e2e13dbf83b8bc331b6effa75143930b4892.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096673 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-db1a0a35-4ef3-5f5a-8985-ee685a957f6e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096460 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](images/cd/cd75b39fc76773c0b3938ab6d60651e2b08dcd9ac325cc05718837934130ea07.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](images/93/933b897b7bc067610c87ea50a6fb871f04c5cc4610bd5bb0c868e6ffbac25e86.svg)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/42/42a1d61517661ccff31d9e603df548e79db7b0674a1f7f34c269a3a19e1c4bd6.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096937 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 25\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=19 \\\\  & y+2z=13 \\\\  & z=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(5)=13\\,⟹\\,y=13-10=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=3$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(3)+2(5)=19\\,⟹\\,x=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=6,y=3$, and $z=5.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨6,3,5⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-145fd237-737e-5055-9883-501b0228a34c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-145fd237-737e-5055-9883-501b0228a34c" :answer-field/id #uuid "145fd237-737e-5055-9883-501b0228a34c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a48bd680-d71c-5a27-9b6b-4fee3480952d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c64960b9-232a-5479-96de-e63c3bb0d15f" "answer-3faa2fb1-77d5-521f-acea-30296fef736c" "answer-797daa95-425d-5598-93a6-9f8e22458433" "answer-2af7fa69-5175-5f82-abdc-7a83d1c7437a" "answer-a48bd680-d71c-5a27-9b6b-4fee3480952d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c64960b9-232a-5479-96de-e63c3bb0d15f" :answer/id #uuid "c64960b9-232a-5479-96de-e63c3bb0d15f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,2,5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3faa2fb1-77d5-521f-acea-30296fef736c" :answer/id #uuid "3faa2fb1-77d5-521f-acea-30296fef736c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-797daa95-425d-5598-93a6-9f8e22458433" :answer/id #uuid "797daa95-425d-5598-93a6-9f8e22458433" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,2,5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2af7fa69-5175-5f82-abdc-7a83d1c7437a" :answer/id #uuid "2af7fa69-5175-5f82-abdc-7a83d1c7437a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,3,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a48bd680-d71c-5a27-9b6b-4fee3480952d" :answer/id #uuid "a48bd680-d71c-5a27-9b6b-4fee3480952d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,3,5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-db1a0a35-4ef3-5f5a-8985-ee685a957f6e" :question/id #uuid "db1a0a35-4ef3-5f5a-8985-ee685a957f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73593" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+6y-3z=-1 \\\\  & -2x-12y+8z=1 \\\\  & -x-5y+4z=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8fa000c8-106a-5c36-ab34-ed3791f10731"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8fa000c8-106a-5c36-ab34-ed3791f10731" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa000c8-106a-5c36-ab34-ed3791f10731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48cbaac4-0396-5dd0-87a0-2f04eaf0760f" "answer-979ac4ef-5db7-5cde-816c-7fb542951f8b" "answer-70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" "answer-8b765cfb-d1ea-559d-a6ff-8457bb546f81" "answer-1111935c-e645-5bcc-9a24-5310e4abf00c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48cbaac4-0396-5dd0-87a0-2f04eaf0760f" :answer/id #uuid "48cbaac4-0396-5dd0-87a0-2f04eaf0760f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-979ac4ef-5db7-5cde-816c-7fb542951f8b" :answer/id #uuid "979ac4ef-5db7-5cde-816c-7fb542951f8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b765cfb-d1ea-559d-a6ff-8457bb546f81" :answer/id #uuid "8b765cfb-d1ea-559d-a6ff-8457bb546f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1111935c-e645-5bcc-9a24-5310e4abf00c" :answer/id #uuid "1111935c-e645-5bcc-9a24-5310e4abf00c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097841 :tutorial/content "Consider a system of linear equations and its respective augmented matrix $M\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/67/673ea82819858b9a46e0e351a8d6f41b069ed039ee0d31a382110f938f7ef72a.svg)\n\nWe can reduce $M$ to row echelon form using the standard Gaussian elimination algorithm. The algorithm that we use is very similar to the case of $2 \\times 2$ systems. \n\nOur goal is to create a descending \"staircase\" of $1$'s with $0$'s below, and we achieve this using elementary row operations. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix is now in row echelon form, and we can apply back substitution to solve the original system of equations.\n\n**Note:** The row echelon form of a matrix is *not* unique.  In the previous example, after the second row operation we arrived at\n\n![](images/35/35627a034b30736abb057c01f3251fc047dce780a8cbcf389f8b5c2c2317d766.svg)\n\nThis augmented matrix is already in row echelon form! However, it is always useful to do an extra step and obtain $1$'s along the main diagonal, like we did previously:\n\n![](images/32/32a252e05e299a206f2f3776a2a04419f21726e1f8f542cfd4f328dac3251f21.svg)\n\nHaving $1$'s along the main diagonal makes the final back substitution process a little easier." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096856 :activity/expected-seconds 720.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
